--TEST--
`$x++` and `--$x` are writes, so an increment's target takes the same three refusals a plain assignment's target does — `rule:types/grammar`, `rule:classes/property-hooks`, `rule:types/erased-member-access`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `nvs_ir::lower` desugars an increment into the `$x = $x + 1` a compound
// assignment already becomes, so its target is a write target and nothing
// else: the three places `nvs_types::expr::assign`'s `check_write_target`
// refuses to write a value have no more of a place to put `± 1`. All three
// are asked the same question here — the `?->` whose `null` is not a place,
// the hooked property `rule:classes/property-hooks` makes a pair of accessors rather than a
// slot, and the erased receiver `rule:types/erased-member-access` resolves by name at run time —
// and what this pins is that they *agree* with the answer `=` already gives,
// which no one of them shows on its own line. Prefix and postfix are one arm.
class Plain {
    public int $n;
    public array<int> $counts;

    public function constructor() {
        $this->n = 0;
        array<int> $seed = ["0" => 1];
        $this->counts = $seed;
    }
}

class Grid {
    public array<int> $counts {
        get => $this->counts;
        set (array<int> $v) {
            $this->counts = $v;
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
        array<int> $seed = ["0" => 1];
        $this->counts = $seed;
    }
}

?Plain $maybe = new Plain();
$maybe?->n++;
--$maybe?->n;
// The nullable base a subscript over a refused root reads as is a symptom of
// the `?->`, not a second mistake: `E0482` is held back so this line takes
// the same `E0479` the two above it do.
$maybe?->counts["0"]++;

var $g = new Grid();
$g->counts["0"]++;

object $erased = new Plain();
$erased->counts["0"]++;
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0479]: `?->` cannot be written through
   --> case.nvs:37:1
%A
error[E0479]: `?->` cannot be written through
   --> case.nvs:38:3
%A
error[E0479]: `?->` cannot be written through
   --> case.nvs:42:1
%A
error[E0478]: an array element cannot be written through the hooked property `counts`
   --> case.nvs:45:1
%A
error[E0480]: an array element cannot be written through the erased property `counts`
   --> case.nvs:48:1
%A
